+// left quarter. Has no effect outside main_only. A screen should call this
+// itself if it wants its overlay content resized/repositioned - it isn't
+// automatic.
+void SIM_SetMainOnlyOverlayTransform(float scale, float anchorX, float anchorY);
+
+// Strips the white matte from the SUB engine's composited overlay content.
+// Much of this game's 2D art was anti-aliased against an opaque light
+// background, leaving near-white pixels baked into its silhouette; harmless on
+// hardware, where the art has its own light backdrop behind it, but a visible
+// halo once the art is composited over a dark scene in main_only. When enabled,
+// silhouette pixels that are essentially greyscale get their alpha reduced by
+// how light they are, so the matte fades out while genuine art colors keep full
+// opacity. Off by default, no effect outside main_only. Enable it per screen.
+void SIM_SetMainOnlyOverlayDefringe(BOOL enable);
